(HTML from Scratch) Tj T*
(Course summary | Instructor: Dave Gray) Tj T*
T*
(A short summary of the course: the structure of a web page, from text and links to semantic tags,) Tj T*
(tables and forms.) Tj T*
T*
(Week 1-2) Tj T*
(Getting Started) Tj T*
(HTML describes structure using elements made of tags. A page starts with <!DOCTYPE html>, then) Tj T*
(<html lang="en"> containing <head> and <body>. Save the file as .html and open it in a) Tj T*
(browser.) Tj T*
T*
(Head and Text) Tj T*
(The <head> holds the <title>, <meta charset="utf-8"> and the viewport meta tag. In the) Tj T*
(body use headings h1 to h6 \(one h1 per page\), paragraphs p, strong and em.) Tj T*
T*
(Lists and Links) Tj T*
(Use ul for bullet lists, ol for numbered lists and li for items. Links use <a href="..."> with clear) Tj T*
(text. With target="_blank" also add rel="noopener".) Tj T*
T*
(Images) Tj T*
(Use <img src alt width height>. The alt text describes the image \(leave it empty for) Tj T*
(decorative images\). Width and height prevent layout shifts, and loading="lazy" delays offscreen) Tj T*
(images.) Tj T*
T*
(Week 3-4) Tj T*
(Semantic Tags) Tj T*
(header, nav, main, article, section, aside and footer describe the meaning of content.) Tj T*
(They help accessibility and SEO. Use div only when no semantic tag fits.) Tj T*
T*
(Tables) Tj T*
(Tables use table, tr, th and td, grouped with thead and tbody, and a caption. Use tables for) Tj T*
(data, never for layout. The scope attribute on th helps screen readers.) Tj T*
T*
(Forms and Inputs) Tj T*
(A form contains inputs. Link each label to its field with for and id. Input types include text,) Tj T*
(email, password and checkbox. Add name so the value is submitted, and required for) Tj T*
(validation.) Tj T*
T*
(Final Project) Tj T*
(Combine everything in one page: a header with navigation, main content, an image, a list or table, a) Tj T*
(contact form and a footer. Check heading order and alt text, then validate the HTML.) Tj T*
T*
(Quick reference) Tj T*
(<a href>                              Create a link) Tj T*
(<img alt>                             Image with a description) Tj T*
ET
